1
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:17,320
Casting their ballots to decide who should hold the seat that has been held by the likes of Tina Smith,
人们投下选票，决定由谁接任这个席位；蒂娜·史密斯，

2
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:22,380
Al Franken, Paul Wellstone, Walter Mondale, and Hubert Humphrey.
阿尔·弗兰肯、保罗·韦尔斯通、沃尔特·蒙代尔和休伯特·汉弗莱，都曾担任过它。

3
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:38,510
But this seat was also once held by a man named Knute Nelson, who passed a bill more than a century ago that forced thousands of Anishinaabe people from their land and
但这个席位，也曾属于克努特·纳尔逊。一百多年前，他通过的一项法案，迫使成千上万阿尼希纳贝人离开自己的土地，

4
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,770
Onto the White Earth Reservation.
迁入白土保留地。

5
00:00:41,390 --> 00:00:56,680
And tonight, a daughter of the White Earth Nation has been elected to occupy that same seat as the first Native American woman ever elected to the United States Senate.
而今晚，一位白土部族的女儿，当选担任同一个席位，成为史上首位当选美国参议员的原住民女性。

6
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:12,040
Please welcome my wife, my person, and our Senator-elect, Peggy Flanagan!
请欢迎我的妻子、我的伴侣、我们的候任参议员，佩吉·弗拉纳根！

7
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:47,411
Woo!
太棒了！

8
00:01:55,281 --> 00:02:03,786
Woo!
太棒了！

9
00:02:03,796 --> 00:02:10,991
Minnesota!
明尼苏达！

10
00:02:31,812 --> 00:02:34,571
Wow!
哇！

11
00:02:34,581 --> 00:02:39,282
All right.
好了。

12
00:02:39,292 --> 00:02:41,162
All right.
好了。

13
00:02:41,172 --> 00:02:44,396
Minnesota!
明尼苏达！

14
00:02:44,406 --> 00:02:52,210
You just beat Donald Trump again!
你们刚刚又一次击败了唐纳德·特朗普！

15
00:02:59,090 --> 00:02:59,930
And you know what?
你们知道吗？

16
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:02,990
America did, too.
美国也一样。

17
00:03:04,057 --> 00:03:09,860
You said no more war.
你们说，不要再有战争。

18
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,540
No more health care cuts.
不要再削减医疗保障。

19
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:17,580
No more taking food away from children and seniors.
不要再夺走儿童和老人餐桌上的食物。

20
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:24,380
No more selling this country off to the highest bidder.
不要再把这个国家卖给出价最高的人。

21
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:34,870
And you said no more masked goons shooting our neighbors and terrorizing our communities.
你们说，不要再让蒙面暴徒向邻居开枪、恐吓我们的社区。

22
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:47,240
You said no more ballrooms, no more bombs or tax breaks for billionaires.
不要再修宴会厅，不要再投炸弹，不要再给亿万富翁减税。

23
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:55,420
The grift stops now.
中饱私囊，到此为止。

24
00:03:56,457 --> 00:04:11,480
And taking back our country from the grip of the most corrupt administration in our nation's history starts tonight.
今晚开始，我们要把国家从美国历史上最腐败的政府手中夺回来。

25
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:25,640
Because all across this state and all across this country, people are saying enough is enough.
因为全州、全国各地的人都在说：够了，就是够了。

26
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:39,620
They're saying that working people deserve an economy and a country that finally works for them, not Donald Trump and his billionaire besties.
劳动人民值得拥有一个真正为他们运转的经济和国家，而不是只为特朗普和他的亿万富翁好友服务。

27
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:47,370
It is time to end the Trump era of chaos, cruelty, and corruption.
是时候结束特朗普这个混乱、残酷、腐败的时代。

28
00:04:48,450 --> 00:04:57,030
And friends, it is time for new voices to shake up our party and take back our nation.
朋友们，是时候让新的声音撼动我们的政党，夺回我们的国家。

29
00:04:57,030 --> 00:05:04,480
It is time to help people.
是时候帮助人民。

30
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,180
It is time to help people afford the lives they want to live.
帮助人民负担得起自己想过的生活。

31
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:19,020
Let today be the start of a new American movement.
让今天成为一场新的美国运动的起点。

32
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:33,460
It is a movement that is defined not by corporate greed or political hatred, but by the power of people coming together to demand change.
定义这场运动的，不是企业贪婪或政治仇恨，而是人们团结起来、要求改变的力量。

33
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:39,420
And we saw it coming, Minnesota.
明尼苏达，我们早已看到它的到来。

34
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:44,120
Because it began right here.
因为它就从这里开始。

35
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:55,360
When a president who thinks he's a king sent thugs to our state, you sent his private army packing.
当那个自以为是国王的总统，把暴徒派到我们州时，你们把他的私人军队赶了回去。

36
00:05:57,870 --> 00:06:05,110
In the dead of winter, you chose to leave the safety of your home.
严冬之中，你们选择走出安全的家。

37
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:09,570
You picked up groceries for people you didn't know.
为素不相识的人采购食品。

38
00:06:11,290 --> 00:06:14,430
You walked kids to school who weren't yours.
护送并非自己孩子的孩子上学。

39
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:16,350
You marched.
你们走上街头。

40
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:18,130
You blew whistles.
你们吹响哨子。

41
00:06:19,470 --> 00:06:23,590
You believed that your neighbors are always worth fighting for.
你们相信，邻居永远值得我们为之奋斗。

42
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:37,840
And you proved that when Minnesotans fight for one another, we can inspire a nation to join that fight.
你们证明，明尼苏达人为彼此而战时，能鼓舞整个国家加入。

43
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:43,340
Because when you come for one of us, you come for all of us.
因为当你伤害我们中的一个人，就是在伤害我们所有人。

44
00:06:50,135 --> 00:07:09,074
And And we are not just the land of 10,000 lakes.
我们不只是“万湖之州”。

45
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:14,210
We are the land of 5.8 million neighbors.
我们也是五百八十万邻人的家园。

46
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:22,810
And to be a Minnesotan is to believe in fairness above all else.
作为明尼苏达人，就是相信公平高于一切。

47
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:25,730
It moves us to act for one another.
这推动着我们为彼此行动。

48
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:29,170
And today, we chose change.
而今天，我们选择了改变。

49
00:07:33,055 --> 00:07:41,670
All across the country today, people spoke loudly and clearly, and the powerful sure better listen.
今天，全国人民清楚、响亮地发出了声音，权势者最好认真倾听。

50
00:07:43,430 --> 00:08:04,150
Whether the people put up signs for a pediatrician in South Carolina or made calls for a former school teacher in Texas whether they knocked on doors for a Paralympic legislator in
无论是为南卡罗来纳的一位儿科医生插上支持标牌，为得州的一位前教师打电话，还是为艾奥瓦的一位残奥运动员州议员，

51
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:21,500
Iowa or for a logger in Maine, a Methodist minister in Kansas, or a Muslim American doctor in Michigan,
为缅因州的伐木工、堪萨斯的循道宗牧师，或密歇根的穆斯林美国医生敲门，

52
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:52,511
Or whether they voted for the daughter of a Navy veteran and school teacher in Chicago, or worked their hearts out for this Irish Catholic Native American from St. Louis Park.
无论是投票给芝加哥一位海军老兵与教师的女儿，还是为我这个来自圣路易斯帕克、信奉天主教、有爱尔兰血统的原住民女性竭尽全力。

53
00:08:52,521 --> 00:09:01,780
We know We know that people demanded more.
我们知道，人民要求更多。

54
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:08,280
And for those of us elected in this moment, it is our duty to deliver.
对我们这些此刻当选的人来说，兑现承诺，是责任。

55
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:13,770
And you better believe that change is going to come.
请你们相信，改变一定会到来。

56
00:09:14,210 --> 00:09:20,070
It's going to come from new voices that weren't picked by the establishment or party leaders.
它将来自那些不是由建制势力、不是由党内领袖挑选的新声音。

57
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:27,670
We were picked by the people.
我们是人民选出来的。

58
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:34,820
We fought back against the money.
我们反击了金钱势力。

59
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:42,460
We took on our own party, and we are the ones who are going to shake up the status quo.
我们挑战了自己党内的力量，而我们正是将要撼动现状的人。

60
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:54,750
We were overlooked and underestimated, but we will not be stopped.
我们曾被忽视、被低估，但不会被阻挡。

61
00:10:11,257 --> 00:10:13,208
Boozhoo.
你好。（奥吉布瓦语）

62
00:10:13,218 --> 00:10:16,008
Peggy Flanagan Anishinaabe Kwe.
我是佩吉·弗拉纳根，一位阿尼希纳贝女性。

63
00:10:16,018 --> 00:10:33,910
[Speaks in Ojibwe.] So, the name you voted for on the ballot says Peggy Flanagan.
[用奥吉布瓦语自我介绍。]你们在选票上看到的名字，是佩吉·弗拉纳根。

64
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:39,290
But, my Ojibwe name is Speaks in a loud and clear voice woman.
但我的奥吉布瓦名字，意为“声音响亮清晰的女人”。

65
00:10:39,942 --> 00:10:50,370
I am a proud daughter of the White Earth Nation.
我是白土部族骄傲的女儿。

66
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:56,300
And my family is the wolf clan.
我的家族属于狼氏族。

67
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:02,860
And the role of our clan is to ensure we never leave anyone behind.
我们氏族的职责，是确保不落下任何人。

68
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:07,280
And that's been the purpose of our campaign.
这也一直是我们竞选的宗旨。

69
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:12,520
We refuse to let this country leave anyone behind.
我们拒绝让这个国家抛下任何人。

70
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,020
And here's the deal.
事情是这样的。

71
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:20,400
Our campaign didn't begin in a Washington, D.C.
我们的竞选，不是从华盛顿的

72
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:21,520
Conference room.
会议室开始的。

73
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:25,580
But, at a kitchen table in St. Louis Park.
而是从圣路易斯帕克的一张厨房餐桌开始。

74
00:11:28,110 --> 00:11:29,190
And it grew.
随后，它不断壮大。

75
00:11:30,170 --> 00:11:36,110
It grew in the basement of the Hibbing Public Library next to the Bob Dylan exhibit.
在希宾公共图书馆的地下室、鲍勃·迪伦展览旁，生根成长。

76
00:11:36,110 --> 00:11:48,708
In cafes, in churches, in VFWs, barns, garages, union halls, and living rooms.
在咖啡馆、教堂、退伍军人会馆、谷仓、车库、工会大厅和客厅里。

77
00:11:50,790 --> 00:12:00,110
And at the darkest hour, in the weeks and months after Donald Trump was elected, when he still looked unbeatable,
最黑暗的时刻，特朗普当选后的那些日子里，当他看上去仍不可战胜时，

78
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:04,190
You took the boldest action imaginable.
你们采取了最勇敢的行动。

79
00:12:04,830 --> 00:12:06,770
You showed up.
你们站了出来。

80
00:12:06,770 --> 00:12:12,430
And we took out our flip chart paper.
我们拿出挂图纸。

81
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:16,170
And we asked each other, "What worries you?
问彼此：“你在担心什么？

82
00:12:17,010 --> 00:12:18,510
Who are you fighting for?
你在为谁奋斗？

83
00:12:19,090 --> 00:12:21,130
And what brings you hope?"
什么让你心怀希望？”

84
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:26,110
And we even put it on Post-it notes and we shared our stories.
我们把答案写在便利贴上，分享自己的故事。

85
00:12:27,210 --> 00:12:33,950
And people all across this state have continued to share their stories with me every day since.
从那以后，全州的人们每天都在继续与我分享。

86
00:12:36,690 --> 00:12:48,657
Like Jessica, a librarian married to a farmer in Canby, who has a $16,000 deductible and had to pay 600 bucks for a 5-minute med check.
例如坎比的图书管理员杰西卡，她嫁给一位农民，保险自付额高达一万六千美元，五分钟的用药检查却要花六百美元。

87
00:12:49,140 --> 00:13:01,680
Or Maggie in Moorhead, who works the night shift at a hotel and then gets up in the morning to run a bakery the next day because one job isn't enough.
又如穆尔黑德的玛吉，在酒店上夜班，早晨又得起床经营面包店，因为一份工作不够维持生活。

88
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:03,760
It should be.
本来，一份就应该够。

89
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:16,370
Or my buddy Bentley, who I met in Brainerd, who relies on Medicaid to survive.
还有在布雷纳德认识的小朋友本特利，他靠医疗补助维持生命。

90
00:13:17,290 --> 00:13:23,650
His mom, Chris, lives in fear of what Donald Trump's cuts to Medicaid will mean for her child.
他的母亲克里斯，总在担心特朗普削减医疗补助会怎样影响自己的孩子。

91
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:28,570
And she is one of the best moms I have ever met in my entire life.
她是我一生见过最好的母亲之一。

92
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:36,090
It is the people of Minnesota that saw a space to fight back in this campaign.
是明尼苏达人民，在这场竞选中看到了反击的空间。

93
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:40,330
You powered us to victory and you made our mission clear.
你们推动我们走向胜利，也明确了我们的使命。

94
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:45,030
You fought for me and now I'm going to fight for you.
你们为我而战，现在，我将为你们而战。

95
00:13:47,929 --> 00:13:57,110
So, friends, in Washington, here's what I'm going to throw down for.
朋友们，到华盛顿后，我要全力争取这些事。

96
00:13:57,110 --> 00:14:02,620
We are going to lower costs so that families can afford their lives.
降低生活成本，让家庭能够负担生活。

97
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:11,401
We are going to get rid of prior authorizations so that some dude behind a desk, or worse yet,
取消医疗事先审批，让坐在办公桌后的人，甚至更糟，

98
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:18,500
An AI bot, can't determine whether or not you get the life-saving health care that your doctor has prescribed.
一个 AI 机器人，无法决定你是否能获得医生开出的救命医疗服务。

99
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:27,630
We will pass right to repair so that farmers can fix their own damn equipment.
通过维修权法，让农民有权修理自己的设备。

100
00:14:27,850 --> 00:14:35,800
We will rip ICE apart.
我们要拆解移民与海关执法局。

101
00:14:50,381 --> 00:14:58,931
That's right.
没错。

102
00:14:58,941 --> 00:15:08,980
And we have the opportunity to replace it with an immigration system that is grounded in public safety for everybody.
我们有机会，用一个立足于所有人公共安全的新移民制度取代它。

103
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:17,370
Dignity and due process, which by the way is still a part of our constitution.
维护尊严和正当程序；顺便提醒，这些仍是宪法的一部分。

104
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:27,690
A system that does not tear children away from their families.
一个不会把孩子从家人身边撕开的制度。

105
00:15:28,170 --> 00:15:39,420
We will stop Washington's corruption and hold the most corrupt administration in our nation's history accountable every day.
我们将制止华盛顿的腐败，每一天都追究这个史上最腐败政府的责任。

106
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:46,660
And we will end Donald Trump's reckless war in Iran.
结束特朗普在伊朗发动的鲁莽战争。

107
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:52,630
And hear me now.
请听清楚。

108
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:58,150
We will pass Medicare for All once and for all.
我们将通过全民医疗保险，彻底落实。

109
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:05,700
And listen.
还有，请听着。

110
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:13,700
People will tell us that we are dreaming too big and that we are asking for too much.
有人会说，我们的梦想太大、要求太多。

111
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,916
Do not listen to that.
不要听这些话。

112
00:16:17,926 --> 00:16:26,020
All of this is possible, friends, because we know that we get what we organize for.
朋友们，这一切都可能，因为我们知道，组织起来争取什么，就能赢得什么。

113
00:16:39,182 --> 00:16:40,841
I love you, too.
我也爱你。

114
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:54,790
And I have to say that I can't quite believe that I am standing here as your next United States Senator from the best state in the country.
我必须说，我还是难以相信，自己竟然站在这里，成为全国最棒的州的下一任美国参议员。

115
00:17:05,086 --> 00:17:26,500
My heart My heart My heart is so full.
我的内心，充满了感动。

116
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,700
And I'm also thinking a lot about my mom.
我也一直在想我的母亲。

117
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:37,860
We lost her shortly after the 2022 election.
二〇二二年选举后不久，她离开了我们。

118
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:47,380
And while she hasn't been on this earthly plane, she has been right here with me along this entire journey.
尽管她已不在人世，这整段旅程中，她始终与我同在。

119
00:17:47,380 --> 00:18:04,490
It's Pat Flanagan's strength and resilience that gave me the courage and the conviction to believe that a kid like me could one day stand on a stage like this one.
正是帕特·弗拉纳根的坚强与韧性，给我勇气和信念，让我相信，像我这样的孩子，有一天也能站在这样的舞台上。

120
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:15,760
And it was my dad, Marvin Manypenny, who taught me to speak truth to power.
是我的父亲马文·曼尼彭尼，教会我向权力说真话。

121
00:18:17,610 --> 00:18:22,870
He used to say, "My girl, I want to burn the system down.
他常说：“女儿啊，我想把这套体制烧掉。

122
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:27,570
And you want to change it from the inside out."
而你想从内部改变它。”

123
00:18:28,490 --> 00:18:31,430
Well, Minnesota, that's what we did tonight.
明尼苏达，今晚，我们就是这样做的。

124
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:40,260
And that is what we are going to keep doing together.
我们也将继续一起这样做。

125
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:46,300
We're going to change the hell out of the system and finally make it work for us.
彻底改变这套体制，终于让它为我们服务。

126
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:59,640
Because you proved that once again, the many can beat the money, and no president can ever beat the power of the people.
你们再次证明，广大民众能够战胜金钱，没有任何总统能战胜人民的力量。

127
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:09,460
You said, loud and clear, that we refuse to settle for leftovers.
你们清楚、响亮地说，我们拒绝只分到残羹剩饭。

128
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:28,400
And you you helped a small, but scrappy, often underestimated, enrolled member of the White Earth Nation become the first Native American woman in history to be elected to the United States Senate.
你们帮助一个身材小巧、却顽强不屈、常被低估的白土部族成员，成为史上第一位当选美国参议员的原住民女性。

129
00:19:49,423 --> 00:20:07,900
So, to the young people out there who look like me, to the daughters and to the sons who too often are forgotten or erased,
那些和我长得相像的年轻人，那些常被遗忘、被抹去的女儿与儿子们，

130
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:10,660
I see you.
我看见你们了。

131
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:20,390
Do not be disheartened that it took 250 years for one of us to get here.
不要因为过了二百五十年，我们才有一人走到这里，就灰心。

132
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:34,960
Be inspired by the fact that with grit and determination and the resilience of our people, whichever one of you is next,
要从这里获得鼓舞：凭借毅力、决心，以及我们人民的韧性，无论下一个是你们中的谁，

133
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:37,520
You're going to get here a lot faster.
你都会更快走到这里。

134
00:20:38,619 --> 00:20:49,360
Because if Auntie Peggy can do it, you can do it, too.
因为佩吉阿姨做得到，你也做得到。

135
00:20:54,520 --> 00:21:00,440
And people people will underestimate you, my girl.
孩子，人们会低估你。

136
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:02,400
Do not let them.
不要让他们这样做。

137
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:04,060
You know who you are.
你知道自己是谁。

138
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:07,440
You know where you come from, and you know what you can do.
知道自己从哪里来，知道自己能做到什么。

139
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:11,280
There is no stopping you from achieving your dreams.
没有什么能阻止你实现梦想。

140
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:22,400
And there is no stopping Minnesota because our cause is righteous and our people will not bend.
也没有什么能阻止明尼苏达，因为我们的事业是正义的，我们的人民不会屈服。

141
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:28,700
And you better believe that we are going to fight like hell for our state and for our country.
请相信，我们一定会为自己的州、自己的国家，全力战斗。

142
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:40,260
And it would take me weeks to thank all of the people that I need to thank.
如果要感谢所有需要感谢的人，我恐怕得花上好几个星期。

143
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,840
But I do want to take a few moments.
但我还是想用一点时间。

144
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:50,720
I want to take a moment to thank Michele Tafoya for running a spirited campaign.
感谢米歇尔·塔福亚，她进行了一场充满活力的竞选。

145
00:21:53,305 --> 00:21:57,975
She No, no, no, no, no.
不，不，不要这样。

146
00:21:57,985 --> 00:22:02,730
She called earlier tonight, and she said, "I hope you do right by Minnesota."
今晚早些时候，她来电说：“希望你为明尼苏达做正确的事。”

147
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:05,390
And I said, "You bet."
我回答：“那当然。”

148
00:22:09,910 --> 00:22:26,960
I want to thank my campaign team led by a badass Minnesotan from New Ulm who ran a small but mighty team that held 360 events in 125 communities.
感谢竞选团队，由来自新阿尔姆的一位了不起的明尼苏达人领导；这支小而精悍的团队，在一百二十五个社区举办了三百六十场活动。

149
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:33,656
And she did it.
她做到了。

150
00:22:33,656 --> 00:22:41,940
She did it in the face of unimaginable tragedies and unprecedented money spent against us.
面对难以想象的悲剧，以及对手投入的空前资金，她仍然做到了。

151
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,660
Thank you, Peyton Lewis.
谢谢你，佩顿·刘易斯。

152
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:52,580
And thank you to the campaign team that you led to victory.
也感谢你带领取得胜利的竞选团队。

153
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:54,620
You slayed.
你们太厉害了。

154
00:22:54,620 --> 00:23:18,060
And to Megan Shannon, our deputy campaign manager, whose problem-solving abilities know no bounds and can always solve problems and knows which direction flags should face.
感谢副竞选经理梅根·香农，你解决问题的能力无穷无尽，总能找到办法，连旗帜该朝哪个方向都知道。

155
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:22,400
I thank you so much.
非常感谢你。

156
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:25,580
And to Noodle, we can't wait to meet you.
还有努德尔，我们迫不及待想见到你。

157
00:23:25,580 --> 00:23:37,840
And to every single volunteer whose hard work powered this entire campaign, thank you.
每一位用辛勤劳动支撑整场竞选的志愿者，谢谢你们。

158
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:38,640
Thank you.
谢谢。

159
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:39,480
Thank you.
谢谢。

160
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:44,800
And thank you, Senator Tina Smith.
感谢蒂娜·史密斯参议员。

161
00:23:47,916 --> 00:24:00,600
Thank you for being a mentor and a friend and an inspiration.
感谢你做我的导师、朋友，给予我启发。

162
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:05,980
Thank you for everything you've done for me and for the people of Minnesota.
感谢你为我、为明尼苏达人民所做的一切。

163
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:14,920
You are leaving some awfully big Chuck Taylors to fill, sister.
姐妹，你留下的那双匡威帆布鞋，实在太难接过了。

164
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:17,120
I love you so much.
我非常爱你。

165
00:24:18,980 --> 00:24:23,931
And thank you to Governor Tim Walz.
也感谢蒂姆·沃尔兹州长。

166
00:24:23,931 --> 00:24:35,390
I am grateful for all of the work that we did together on behalf of Minnesota's children and families and the historic work to strengthen tribal state relations.
感谢我们共同为明尼苏达儿童与家庭所做的工作，也感谢在加强部族与州政府关系上取得的历史性成果。

167
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:38,670
Thank you, Governor, for your service to Minnesota.
州长，谢谢你为明尼苏达的服务。

168
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:54,550
And last, but never, ever least, Tom and Siobhan, you are my inspiration.
最后，当然绝非最不重要的，汤姆和希沃恩，你们是我的动力。

169
00:24:56,090 --> 00:24:57,390
Tom, you are my person.
汤姆，你是我的灵魂伴侣。

170
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:03,660
And I cannot believe I got to marry my local celebrity crush.
我仍不敢相信，自己竟然嫁给了曾经暗恋的本地名人。

171
00:25:06,770 --> 00:25:11,830
And that every day you define what it means to be in a true partnership.
每一天，你都让我明白，真正的伙伴关系意味着什么。

172
00:25:12,330 --> 00:25:12,990
I love you.
我爱你。

173
00:25:20,347 --> 00:25:32,660
And to my whole heart, Siobhan, my girl, I am so proud of you every single day.
还有我的全部心肝，希沃恩，我的女儿，每一天，我都为你骄傲。

174
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,500
You know who you are.
你知道自己是谁。

175
00:25:35,940 --> 00:25:42,500
Your talent, your heart, your courage, your compassion, your humor knows no bounds.
你的才华、真心、勇气、同情心和幽默，无穷无尽。

176
00:25:44,140 --> 00:25:50,360
And my proudest accomplishment ever was bringing you into the world and being your mom.
我最骄傲的成就，就是把你带到这个世界，成为你的母亲。

177
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:52,000
I love you so much, my girl.
我非常爱你，我的女儿。

178
00:26:00,170 --> 00:26:07,423
And tonight, it's hard not to think about my political hero, Paul Wellstone.
今晚，很难不想起我的政治英雄，保罗·韦尔斯通。

179
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:13,030
Paul's last campaign was my first.
保罗最后一次竞选，正是我第一次参与竞选。

180
00:26:14,050 --> 00:26:18,170
And he used to always say, "I don't represent the big oil companies.
他常常说：“我不代表大型石油公司。

181
00:26:18,730 --> 00:26:21,450
I don't represent the big pharmaceutical companies.
不代表大型制药公司。

182
00:26:21,450 --> 00:26:24,770
I don't represent the Enrons of the world.
不代表这个世界上的安然公司。

183
00:26:25,670 --> 00:26:26,230
But you know what?
但你们知道吗？

184
00:26:26,690 --> 00:26:29,530
They already have great representation in Washington.
他们在华盛顿早已拥有很好的代表。

185
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:34,150
It's the rest of the people that need it.
需要代表的，是其他普通人。

186
00:26:34,150 --> 00:26:35,050
I represent the people of Minnesota.
我代表明尼苏达人民。”

187
00:26:37,970 --> 00:26:42,090
And so, I will say it the way that Paul did.
所以，我也要用保罗的方式说这句话。

188
00:26:42,850 --> 00:26:47,010
You will always know where I stand and who I stand up for.
你们始终会知道我的立场，知道我为谁挺身而出。

189
00:26:49,269 --> 00:26:51,630
I won't represent the billionaires.
我不会代表亿万富翁。

190
00:26:52,070 --> 00:26:56,490
I won't represent the big drug companies or the big insurance companies.
不会代表大型药企、大型保险公司。

191
00:26:57,450 --> 00:27:00,790
And I sure as hell won't represent Donald Trump.
更绝不会代表唐纳德·特朗普。

192
00:27:01,798 --> 00:27:09,900
I will represent the people of Minnesota whether you voted for me or not.
我会代表明尼苏达人民，无论你们是否投票给我。

193
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:22,520
Because I have never been more proud to be a Minnesotan than I am right this minute.
因为此时此刻，身为明尼苏达人的自豪感，胜过以往任何时候。

194
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:36,690
And friends, when I get to Washington, I know I'm not going alone.
朋友们，前往华盛顿时，我知道自己不是一个人去。

195
00:27:37,110 --> 00:27:39,250
I am bringing all of you with me.
我会带着你们所有人同行。

196
00:27:44,210 --> 00:27:47,290
Thank you all so much.
非常感谢大家。

197
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:48,402
Gichi migwech.
衷心感谢。（奥吉布瓦语）

198
00:27:48,730 --> 00:27:50,690
I love you, Minnesota.
明尼苏达，我爱你们。